.TH EMAIL\-CLI 1 "" "email-cli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
email\-cli \- terminal email client for IMAP and Gmail (batch mode)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B email\-cli
.RI [ account ]
.RI [ --batch ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B email\-cli
reads and modifies mail over IMAP or the Gmail API from the command line.
It is the read\-write member of the suite: besides listing and reading it can
send, flag, label, move and delete.
.PP
If you need a tool that provably cannot change anything \- for scripts, cron
jobs or AI agents \- use
.BR email\-cli\-ro (1)
instead. For an interactive terminal UI use
.BR email\-tui (1).
.PP
On first run, with no account configured, an interactive setup wizard starts.
It needs a terminal; in a non\-interactive context configure the account first
or the command aborts.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Reading
.TP
.B list
List messages. Unread only by default.
.TP
.BI show " uid " [ \-\-raw ]
Print one message as rendered text, or verbatim with
.BR \-\-raw .
.TP
.B list\-folders
List IMAP folders with counts.
.TP
.B list\-labels
List Gmail labels with IDs.
.TP
.BI list\-attachments " uid"
List a message's attachments.
.TP
.BI save\-attachment " uid filename " [ dir ]
Write an attachment to disk.
.SS Writing
.TP
.B send
Send a message non\-interactively; see
.B email\-cli help send
for the required options.
.TP
.BI mark\-read " uid" "\fR, \fP" mark\-unread " uid"
Toggle the read state.
.TP
.BI mark\-starred " uid" "\fR, \fP" remove\-starred " uid"
Toggle the star / flagged state.
.TP
.BI mark\-junk " uid" "\fR, \fP" mark\-notjunk " uid"
Toggle the junk state.
.TP
.BI add\-label " uid label" "\fR, \fP" remove\-label " uid label"
Gmail: add or remove a label.
.TP
.BI create\-label " name" "\fR, \fP" delete\-label " id"
Gmail: manage labels.
.TP
.BI create\-folder " name" "\fR, \fP" delete\-folder " name"
IMAP: manage folders.
.SS Accounts and rules
.TP
.B list\-accounts ", " add\-account ", " remove\-account " " \fIemail\fP
Manage configured accounts.
.TP
.B config
Show or change configuration, including SMTP.
.TP
.B migrate\-credentials
Re\-encrypt or decrypt stored passwords.
.TP
.B rules list ", " rules apply " [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fP], " rules add ", " rules remove
Manage per\-account sorting rules. See
.BR email\-import\-rules (1)
to import them from Thunderbird.
.TP
.B help " [\fIcommand\fP], " help gmail
Command help; the
.B gmail
topic walks through OAuth2 setup.
.SH OPTIONS
The options of
.B list
and
.BR show ,
the
.B \-\-batch
flag, and the
.B \-\-account
selector behave exactly as described in
.BR email\-cli\-ro (1).
.SH VIRTUAL FOLDERS AND SEARCH
.B \-\-folder
accepts the virtual folders
.BR __unread__ ", " __flagged__ ", " __answered__ ", " __forwarded__ ", "
.B __junk__
and
.BR __phishing__ ,
and the content search
.BR "__search__:<scope>:<query>" .
Both are resolved from the local store and work offline.
See
.BR email\-cli\-ro (1)
for the full description, including why a body search (scope
.BR 3 )
is usually the right choice for order confirmations and other
machine\-generated mail.
.SH FILES
As in
.BR email\-cli\-ro (1).
Configuration is written with mode 0600 and the local store with 0700.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success, non\-zero on failure. Errors go to standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.nf
email\-cli \-\-batch list \-\-folder __unread__
email\-cli \-\-batch list \-\-folder \(dq__search__:3:invoice\(dq
email\-cli mark\-read 0000000000012345 \-\-folder INBOX
email\-cli send \-\-to a@example.com \-\-subject Hi \-\-body \(dqHello\(dq
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR email\-cli\-ro (1),
.BR email\-tui (1),
.BR email\-sync (1),
.BR email\-import\-rules (1)
